{"id":"mahabharata-12-052","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":52,"title":"द्विपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 52 · Krishna asks Bhishma to teach","summary":{"en":"Krishna asks Bhishma to dispel the grief of the king and teach him dharma, since all wisdom will pass away with Bhishma. Bhishma says that he is unable because of the pain of the arrows and the presence of his teacher, but Krishna removes his pain and gives him clear vision.","kn":"ರಾಜನ ಶೋಕ ನಿವಾರಿಸಿ ಧರ್ಮ ಬೋಧಿಸಲು ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಭೀಷ್ಮನಿಗೆ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಷ್ಮನೊಂದಿಗೆ ಎಲ್ಲ ಜ್ಞಾನ ಹೋಗುತ್ತದೆ. ಬಾಣದ ನೋವು, ಗುರುವಿನ ಸನ್ನಿಧಿಯಿಂದ ಹೇಳಲಾರೆನೆಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೃಷ್ಣ ನೋವು ನಿವಾರಿಸಿ ಸ್ಪಷ್ಟ ದೃಷ್ಟಿ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कृष्ण भीष्म से राजा का शोक दूर कर धर्म सिखाने को कहते हैं, क्योंकि भीष्म के साथ सारा ज्ञान चला जाएगा। भीष्म बाणों की पीड़ा और गुरु की उपस्थिति के कारण असमर्थता बताते हैं, पर कृष्ण उनकी पीड़ा हर कर स्पष्ट दृष्टि देते हैं।","te":"రాజు శోకాన్ని తొలగించి ధర్మం బోధించమని కృష్ణుడు భీష్ముని కోరతాడు; భీష్మునితో సర్వ జ్ఞానం పోతుంది. బాణాల నొప్పి, గురువు సన్నిధి వల్ల చెప్పలేనని భీష్ముడు అంటాడు; కృష్ణుడు నొప్పిని తొలగించి స్పష్ట దృష్టిని ఇస్తాడు.","ta":"மன்னரின் துயரை நீக்கித் தர்மத்தைக் கற்பிக்கும்படி கண்ணன் பீஷ்மரைக் கேட்கிறார், பீஷ்மருடன் எல்லா அறிவும் மறையும். அம்பு வலியாலும் குருவின் முன்னிலையாலும் இயலாது என்று பீஷ்மர் கூற, கண்ணன் வலியை நீக்கித் தெளிவான பார்வை அளிக்கிறார்.","ml":"രാജാവിന്റെ ദുഃഖം ശമിപ്പിച്ച് ധർമ്മം പഠിപ്പിക്കാൻ കൃഷ്ണൻ ഭീഷ്മരോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു, കാരണം ഭീഷ്മരോടൊപ്പം എല്ലാ ജ്ഞാനവും നഷ്ടപ്പെടും. അമ്പുകളുടെ വേദനയും ഗുരുവിന്റെ സാന്നിധ്യവും കാരണം തനിക്ക് കഴിയില്ലെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു; എന്നാൽ കൃഷ്ണൻ വേദന നീക്കി അദ്ദേഹത്തിന് വ്യക്തമായ കാഴ്ച നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.52; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः कृष्णस्य तद्वाक्यं धर्मार्थसहितं हितम् ।\nश्रुत्वा शांतनवो भीष्मः प्रत्युवाच कृताञ्जलिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard that beneficial speech of Krishna, full of dharma and purpose, Bhishma son of Shantanu answered with joined palms."}},{"n":2,"text":"लोकनाथ महाबाहो शिव नारायणाच्युत ।\nतव वाक्यमभिश्रुत्य हर्षेणास्मि परिप्लुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the world, mighty-armed, auspicious Narayana, Achyuta, I am flooded with joy at hearing your words."}},{"n":3,"text":"किं चाहमभिधास्यामि वाक्पते तव संनिधौ ।\nयदा वाचोगतं सर्वं तव वाचि समाहितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What can I say in your presence, lord of speech, when everything that speech can reach is contained in your word?"}},{"n":4,"text":"यद्धि किंचित्कृतं लोके कर्तव्यं क्रियते च यत् ।\nत्वत्तस्तन्निःसृतं देव लोका बुद्धिमया हि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever has been done in the world and whatever remains to be done has come forth from you, god; the worlds are made of your understanding."}},{"n":5,"text":"कथयेद्देवलोकं यो देवराजसमीपतः ।\nधर्मकामार्थशास्त्राणां सोऽर्थान्ब्रूयात्तवाग्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who would describe the world of the gods in the presence of the king of the gods might as well speak on the teachings of dharma, desire and wealth before you."}},{"n":6,"text":"शराभिघाताद्व्यथितं मनो मे मधुसूदन ।\nगात्राणि चावसीदन्ति न च बुद्धिः प्रसीदति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana, my mind is shaken by the blows of the arrows, my limbs are sinking, and my intellect does not clear."}},{"n":7,"text":"न च मे प्रतिभा काचिदस्ति किंचित्प्रभाषितुम् ।\nपीड्यमानस्य गोविन्द विषानलसमैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Govinda, tormented by arrows like poison and fire, I have no inspiration to say anything."}},{"n":8,"text":"बलं मेधाः प्रजरति प्राणाः संत्वरयन्ति च ।\nमर्माणि परितप्यन्ते भ्रान्तं चेतस्तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"My strength, my wit and my breath are fading and hurrying away; my vital parts burn and my mind is confused."}},{"n":9,"text":"दौर्बल्यात्सज्जते वाङ्मे स कथं वक्तुमुत्सहे ।\nसाधु मे त्वं प्रसीदस्व दाशार्हकुलनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through weakness my voice falters, so how can I venture to speak? Be gracious to me, delight of the Dasharha line."}},{"n":10,"text":"तत्क्षमस्व महाबाहो न ब्रूयां किंचिदच्युत ।\nत्वत्संनिधौ च सीदेत वाचस्पतिरपि ब्रुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So forgive me, mighty-armed Achyuta; I could say nothing. In your presence even Brihaspati would falter while speaking."}},{"n":11,"text":"न दिशः संप्रजानामि नाकाशं न च मेदिनीम् ।\nकेवलं तव वीर्येण तिष्ठामि मधुसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know neither the directions nor the sky nor the earth; I stand only by your power, Madhusudana."}},{"n":12,"text":"स्वयमेव प्रभो तस्माद्धर्मराजस्य यद्धितम् ।\nतद्ब्रवीह्याशु सर्वेषामागमानां त्वमागमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, lord, say yourself right now whatever is good for the king of dharma, for you are the source of all the scriptures."}},{"n":13,"text":"कथं त्वयि स्थिते लोके शाश्वते लोककर्तरि ।\nप्रब्रूयान्मद्विधः कश्चिद्गुरौ शिष्य इव स्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"How, with you present, the eternal maker of the world, could one like me speak, like a pupil in front of his teacher?"}},{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"उपपन्नमिदं वाक्यं कौरवाणां धुरंधरे ।\nमहावीर्ये महासत्त्वे स्थिते सर्वार्थदर्शिनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"This speech is fitting from you, bearer of the burden of the Kurus, mighty and strong, who sees all that matters."}},{"n":15,"text":"यच्च मामात्थ गाङ्गेय बाणघातरुजं प्रति ।\nगृहाणात्र वरं भीष्म मत्प्रसादकृतं विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ganga's son, as for what you told me about the pain from the arrow-wounds, receive here a boon from me, Bhishma, mighty one, granted by my grace."}},{"n":16,"text":"न ते ग्लानिर्न ते मूर्छा न दाहो न च ते रुजा ।\nप्रभविष्यन्ति गाङ्गेय क्षुत्पिपासे न चाप्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"No faintness, no swooning, no burning, no pain, and neither hunger nor thirst will overpower you, son of Ganga."}},{"n":17,"text":"ज्ञानानि च समग्राणि प्रतिभास्यन्ति तेऽनघ ।\nन च ते क्वचिदासक्तिर्बुद्धेः प्रादुर्भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"All your knowledge will shine out in full, blameless one, and your mind will never become attached to anything."}},{"n":18,"text":"सत्त्वस्थं च मनो नित्यं तव भीष्म भविष्यति ।\nरजस्तमोभ्यां रहितं घनैर्मुक्त इवोडुराट् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your mind will always be set in sattva, Bhishma, free of rajas and tamas, like the moon freed from clouds."}},{"n":19,"text":"यद्यच्च धर्मसंयुक्तमर्थयुक्तमथापि वा ।\nचिन्तयिष्यसि तत्राग्र्या बुद्धिस्तव भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever you ponder, whether bound up with dharma or with worldly gain, your insight into it will be of the highest."}},{"n":20,"text":"इमं च राजशार्दूल भूतग्रामं चतुर्विधम् ।\nचक्षुर्दिव्यं समाश्रित्य द्रक्ष्यस्यमितविक्रम ॥","meaning":{"en":"King among men of unmeasured valor, relying on divine sight you will see this fourfold host of living beings."}},{"n":21,"text":"चतुर्विधं प्रजाजालं संयुक्तो ज्ञानचक्षुषा ।\nभीष्म द्रक्ष्यसि तत्त्वेन जले मीन इवामले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Joined to the eye of knowledge, Bhishma, you will see the fourfold web of creatures as truly as a fish in clear water."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"ततस्ते व्याससहिताः सर्व एव महर्षयः ।\nऋग्यजुःसामसंयुक्तैर्वचोभिः कृष्णमर्चयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the great sages, with Vyasa, honored Krishna with words drawn from the Rig, Yajur and Sama Vedas."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततः सर्वार्तवं दिव्यं पुष्पवर्षं नभस्तलात् ।\nपपात यत्र वार्ष्णेयः सगाङ्गेयः सपाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a divine shower of flowers of every season fell from the sky on the spot where the Vrishni, Ganga's son and the Pandavas were."}},{"n":24,"text":"वादित्राणि च दिव्यानि जगुश्चाप्सरसां गणाः ।\nन चाहितमनिष्टं वा किंचित्तत्र व्यदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Troops of apsarases sang with divine instruments, and nothing hostile or unwelcome was seen there."}},{"n":25,"text":"ववौ शिवः सुखो वायुः सर्वगन्धवहः शुचिः ।\nशान्तायां दिशि शान्ताश्च प्रावदन्मृगपक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A pleasant, pure breeze blew, carrying every fragrance; the directions were calm, and the beasts and birds fell quiet."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततो मुहूर्ताद्भगवान्सहस्रांशुर्दिवाकरः ।\nदहन्वनमिवैकान्ते प्रतीच्यां प्रत्यदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, after a short while, the blessed thousand-rayed sun, maker of day, appeared in the west like a fire burning a lonely forest."}},{"n":27,"text":"ततो महर्षयः सर्वे समुत्थाय जनार्दनम् ।\nभीष्ममामन्त्रयां चक्रू राजानं च युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the great sages rose and took leave of Janardana, of Bhishma, and of King Yudhishthira."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततः प्रणाममकरोत्केशवः पाण्डवस्तथा ।\nसात्यकिः संजयश्चैव स च शारद्वतः कृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Keshava, the Pandava, Satyaki, Sanjaya and Kripa son of Sharadvat made their obeisance."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततस्ते धर्मनिरताः सम्यक्तैरभिपूजिताः ।\nश्वः समेष्याम इत्युक्त्वा यथेष्टं त्वरिता ययुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those sages, devoted to dharma, were duly honored by them, and saying \"We shall meet again tomorrow,\" they hurried off wherever they wished."}},{"n":30,"text":"तथैवामन्त्र्य गाङ्गेयं केशवस्ते च पाण्डवाः ।\nप्रदक्षिणमुपावृत्य रथानारुरुहुः शुभान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise, taking leave of Ganga's son, Keshava and the Pandavas circled him to the right and mounted their fine chariots."}},{"n":31,"text":"ततो रथैः काञ्चनदन्तकूबरै-\nर्महीधराभैः समदैश्च दन्तिभिः ।\nहयैः सुपर्णैरिव चाशुगामिभिः\nपदातिभिश्चात्तशरासनादिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with chariots whose poles were fitted with gold and which looked like mountains, with rutting elephants, with swift horses like Garuda, and with foot-soldiers bearing bows and other arms,"}},{"n":32,"text":"ययौ रथानां पुरतो हि सा चमू-\nस्तथैव पश्चादतिमात्रसारिणी ।\nपुरश्च पश्चाच्च यथा महानदी\nपुरर्क्षवन्तं गिरिमेत्य नर्मदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"the army went on, spread out before the chariots and likewise far behind, like the great river Narmada flowing before and behind the mountain Riksha."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततः पुरस्ताद्भगवान्निशाकरः\nसमुत्थितस्तामभिहर्षयंश्चमूम् ।\nदिवाकरापीतरसास्तथौषधीः\nपुनः स्वकेनैव गुणेन योजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in the east the blessed moon, maker of night, rose, gladdening that army, restoring to the herbs, whose sap the sun had drunk, their own virtues once more."}},{"n":34,"text":"ततः पुरं सुरपुरसंनिभद्युति\nप्रविश्य ते यदुवृषपाण्डवास्तदा ।\nयथोचितान्भवनवरान्समाविश-\nञ्श्रमान्विता मृगपतयो गुहा इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Yadava hero and the Pandavas entered the city, radiant like the city of the gods, and went into their own fine houses, tired like lions entering their caves."}}]}]}